KNOWNBUG libcxx
main.cpp
--cpp20 --unwind 8 --unwinding-assertions --stdlib libc++
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ ranges take: SUCCESS$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
Range-pipe over an array with std::views::take.  Two eras of failure:
originally a hard "conversion from 'signed int [5l]' to
'<<type:auto>>'" CONVERSION ERROR (silent all-templates deduction
failure, resolve with nargs=0, at forward@bind_back.h) -- that root
cause was the `= default` copy-constructor skeleton demanding a
DELETED default constructor of a base/member, fixed per N5008
[class.copy.ctor]/14 with the goto-symex family.  NOW the front end
recovers instead but SILENTLY DROPS the range-for loop and the
assertion from main() (wrong-code: goto-functions show arr/sum decls
then straight SET RETURN VALUE 0), so verification succeeds vacuously.
The desc requires the real assertion to be present and SUCCESS.

2026-09-24: the desc never passed `--stdlib libc++`, so it exercised the
libstdc++ headers -- where the same program (cpp20_ranges_basic) is CORE
now; the flag is added so this test is the libc++ variant it is tagged as.
Under libc++ 18 it still fails: `std::views::take(3)` is
`__range_adaptor_closure_t(std::__bind_back(*this, ...))`, and
`__bind_back`'s trailing `-> decltype(__bind_back_t<...>(...))` /
`__perfect_forward` chain is not resolved (the closure's type stays `auto`,
"function call expects function or function pointer as argument, but got
'<<type:auto>>'"; reduced: `std::__bind_back(fn{}, 3)` alone fails with an
enable_if_t<false> instantiation in <__compare/ordering.h>).

2026-10-05 (round 163w): __bind_back's trailing return type resolves
(cpp20_views_take_bind_back_forward_not_found, CORE); the program now
drops tuple:469/488 __tuple_impl and tuple:713 constructors, the
std::forward<_Up>(__u) pack-expansion failure of
cpp20_libcxx_header_drops/test_functional.desc.

2026-10-09 (round 170): fixed on the way -- const/ref-qualified member
templates (cpp11_const_and_non_const_member_function_templates,
cpp11_ref_qualified_member_functions), inherited constructor templates'
default arguments, __is_constructible with several arguments, folds in
base-specifiers.  Still a CONVERSION ERROR: tuple<int>'s converting
constructor from tuple<int &&> drops its body because
__tuple_sfinae_base::__do_test's `_Trait<_LArgs, _RArgs>::value...'
fails (cpp11_template_template_parameter_in_lockstep_pack_expansion).

2026-10-09 (round 171): __tuple_sfinae_base::__do_test resolves
(cpp11_template_template_parameter_in_lockstep_pack_expansion, CORE), as do
folds over __perfect_forward_impl's _Idx pack and its operator()'s
trailing return types.  std::__bind_back(f, 2)(arr) now computes the right
value, but `arr | take(3)' is still a CONVERSION ERROR: in the
operator| constraint, is_invocable_v<__bind_back_op<1>, _Fn &,
tuple<int> &, int (&)[5]> is false (it is true when asserted directly),
and two tuple:488 __tuple_impl bodies are dropped.

2026-10-10 (round 172): with the nested-instantiation bound raised
(cpp11_nested_instantiations_of_one_class_template), checking
is_invocable on a __bind_back closure no longer breaks the later call,
and `arr | c' through a user-written closure base works.  The real
`arr | std::views::take(3)' is still a CONVERSION ERROR, as is
`invoke_result_t<__bind_back_t<...> &, int (&)[5]>' alone.

2026-10-11 (round 174): `arr | std::views::take(3)' now selects the
range | closure operator (cpp20_constrained_hidden_friend_per_
specialization) and invoke_result_t of the closure resolves.  The range-for
now fails comparing take_view's begin() (int *) with its end(), which CBMC
types as a __sentinel: end() const takes the unsized branch after the view
was built through operator| (reduction in progress).
